This is a known breaking change. Android deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` (API 30+), and .NET 10 MAUI no longer supports it. The modern fix is to react to **window insets** on Android.

### Recommended approach

**1. In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`**, handle the keyboard inset:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Compatibility.Platform.Android;

[Activity(WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustNothing, /* ... */)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge insets handling
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
            Window!.DecorView,
            new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    }

    class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Push content up by keyboard height, or nav bar height when closed
            int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

**2. Disable MAUI's built-in auto-scroll** (it conflicts) in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.UseMauiApp<App>()
    .ConfigureMauiHandlers(handlers =>
    {
#if ANDROID
        Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
#endif
    });
```

**3. Use a simple `Grid` layout** for your chat page:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" Command="{Binding SendCommand}" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

### Why this works

The `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` API is Android's modern replacement for `AdjustResize`. It tells you exactly how tall the keyboard is, and you apply that as bottom padding so your input bar slides up above it. This approach is forward-compatible and works reliably on API 30+.

On **iOS**, `AdjustResize`-style behavior still works by default — no extra code needed.
